1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,823
Boredom feels like nothing. A blank space to be filled.

2
00:00:03,823 --> 00:00:07,246
But inside a bored brain, something surprising happens.

3
00:00:07,246 --> 00:00:12,350
The moment you get bored, your brain switches into one of its most valuable modes.

4
00:00:12,350 --> 00:00:15,338
And the modern world is deleting it, on purpose.

5
00:00:15,938 --> 00:00:21,052
When you stop focusing outward, the brain doesn't shut down. It switches networks.

6
00:00:21,052 --> 00:00:23,797
Scientists call it the default mode network.

7
00:00:23,797 --> 00:00:31,345
This is when your brain replays the past, simulates the future, connects distant ideas, and quietly works on who you are.

8
00:00:31,345 --> 00:00:37,021
Some of the best ideas of your life arrived in the shower, on a long walk, waiting in line.

9
00:00:37,021 --> 00:00:41,200
That wasn't a coincidence. That was the default mode doing its job.

10
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:44,453
Boredom is the entrance fee to that state.

11
00:00:44,453 --> 00:00:50,139
Studies show that people who do a boring task first produce more creative ideas afterward.

12
00:00:50,139 --> 00:00:56,456
The uncomfortable craving you feel when bored? That's the brain demanding raw material to work with.

13
00:00:56,456 --> 00:00:58,288
It's hunger, not malfunction.

14
00:00:58,888 --> 00:01:01,802
Here's what we've done to it: we killed boredom.

15
00:01:01,802 --> 00:01:05,689
Queue? Phone. Bathroom? Phone. Thirty seconds of waiting? Phone.

16
00:01:05,689 --> 00:01:09,211
Every gap gets filled before the default mode can boot up.

17
00:01:09,211 --> 00:01:15,040
Which means the daydreaming machinery is starving while you feel like you have no time to think.

18
00:01:15,040 --> 00:01:20,263
You didn't lose the ability to think. You lost the empty space where thinking happens.

19
00:01:20,863 --> 00:01:24,104
So try a strange prescription: get bored on purpose.

20
00:01:24,104 --> 00:01:29,279
Ten minutes a day with no input. Walk without headphones. Dishes without a podcast.

21
00:01:29,279 --> 00:01:32,895
It will feel terrible at first. That's the hunger talking.

22
00:01:32,895 --> 00:01:35,825
Then something old and wonderful boots back up.

23
00:01:35,825 --> 00:01:40,563
The question is: what would your mind build, if you finally let it be bored?
